#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:2
msgid "alsa interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"`alsa` allows access to raw ALSA audio playback and recording devices. This "
"is equivalent to direct driver access to your audio hardware and may block "
"other applications from recording or playing sound."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"To provide better audio sharing and input and output configuration, it's  "
"recommended that most snaps access audio functionality through the system "
"audio layer, such as PulseAudio, via the {ref}`audio-playback <interfaces-"
"audio-playback-interface>` and {ref}`audio-record <interfaces-audio-record-"
"interface>` interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:8
msgid ""
"However, raw access to ALSA devices using this interface can provide a "
"slight performance advantage with input and output latency and avoid "
"resampling which can reduce audio quality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:10
msgid "<h2 id='heading--example'>Example</h2>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"The musical notation and composition application, [MuseScore](https://"
"snapcraft.io/musescore), is a good example of a snap that uses the ALSA "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:14
msgid "To connect a snap to the ALSA interface, run the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:16
msgid "$ sudo snap connect <snap name>:alsa\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:21
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:23
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:25
msgid ""
"The `alsa` interface is not auto-connected, in part, because not all "
"hardware will multiplex clients and therefore may block audio."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:27
msgid ""
"The _libasound2_ library needs to be included in a snap's `stage-packages`, "
"of the part which uses ALSA, either directly or through some other package "
"which brings it in (or manually compiled)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:29
msgid "<h3 id='heading-code'>Code examples</h3>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:31
msgid ""
"The _snapcraft.yaml_ for MuseScore includes an ALSA interface definition: "
"[https://github.com/pachulo/musescore-snap/blob/master/snap/snapcraft.yaml]"
"(https://github.com/pachulo/musescore-snap/blob/"
"9d328cb48679542180b257e32131bbf23ea8cba0/snap/snapcraft.yaml#L32)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/alsa-interface.md:34
msgid ""
"The source code for this interface is in the *snapd* repository: <https://"
"github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/builtin/alsa.go>"
msgstr ""
